/*
 * f3link - link Fallout 3 PC functions, classes and globals to named functions in
 *          sibling builds (Fallout: New Vegas Xbox 360 PDBs, Skyrim PC MAP), with
 *          tiers calibrated by measurement.
 *
 * usage: f3link --evidence <dir> --recipe <units.json> --out <dir>
 *               [--refs id,id,...] [--skyrim id] [--target id]
 *
 * Inputs (all generated by tools/binscan, tools/pdbdump, tools/mapdump):
 *   <evidence>/<id>/binscan/{features,rtti,vtable,rtti_bases}.tsv  per image
 *   <evidence>/<fnv360 id>/{functions,params,locals,globals}.tsv  PDB dumps
 *   <evidence>/tesv_win/publics.tsv                                Skyrim MAP dump
 * Names come only from those symbol files and from the target's own RTTI/strings.
 *
 * Method (a seeded graph matcher, iterated to a fixed point), per image pair A->B:
 *   anchors      vtable (same RTTI class, equal slot count: slot k <-> slot k)
 *                vtable_prefix (slot counts differ: the prefix inherited from a base
 *                  whose slot count agrees on both sides)
 *                ustr (literal referenced by exactly one function on each side)
 *                uvref / uconst / uimport (same with vtable/typedesc refs, large
 *                  constants, imports)
 *                hash (normalized code hash, x86<->x86 only, unique, >= 24 bytes)
 *                strset (string-set Jaccard >= 0.8 over >= 3 strings, mutual best)
 *   propagation  call_seq (callee lists of a linked pair, same length, position-wise)
 *                call_dedup (same on first-occurrence-deduplicated lists)
 *                call_gap (gaps of equal length between already-linked callees)
 *                caller (linked callers all share exactly one unlinked callee)
 *                ustr_rel (a literal with k users on both sides, k-1 already linked
 *                  consistently)
 *   phase 2      objrun (gap between two linked pairs that are neighbours in one
 *                  reference .obj, equal gap counts) and objrun_prop (everything
 *                  propagated after the first objrun link)
 *   Every candidate set is resolved by mutual-best voting (anchors: winner needs
 *   >= 2x (vtables 3x) the runner-up's votes on both sides; propagation: unanimity),
 *   and propagated pairs must not contradict (size ratio 0.33..3, string/vtable-ref
 *   sets compatible).
 *
 * Calibration: the same algorithm is run Skyrim (x86) -> FNV360 0822 retail (PPC);
 * both are named, so precision per method is name equality.  A holdout run hides
 * the anchors of half of the A functions and measures whether propagation recovers
 * them with the same partner (on the calibration pair and on F3 -> FNV360).
 * Tiers: high >= 99%, medium >= 90%, else low (fewer than 20 measured: low).
 *
 * Outputs in <out>: functions.tsv classes.tsv globals.tsv params.tsv calibration.md
 * summary.md.  Reads evidence only; writes nothing but those tables.
 */
#define _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS
